Fix a real upstream gap (not an AXOS feature): get_ASUS_privacy_policy_state()
is declared in shared/shared.h and called from both aws-iot/src/awsiot.c and
uploader/src/uploader.c, but has no implementation anywhere in this Merlin
release's source tree, and no GT-AX6000 prebuilt object provides it either.
Confirmed via a real build attempt: `make gt-ax6000` fails linking aws-iot
with "undefined reference to `get_ASUS_privacy_policy_state'" (uploader/
hadn't been reached yet at that point, but has the identical call and would
hit the same failure).

Fix: replace both calls with a literal `0` (== the function's presumed
"not granted" return value), the conservative default for an unimplemented
privacy-consent check:
- aws-iot/src/awsiot.c: part of `(ASUS_EULA==1) || (get_ASUS_privacy_policy_state(...)==1)`
  — falls back to the ASUS_EULA check alone, the other half of the OR.
- uploader/src/uploader.c: part of an AND chain gating a data-transfer
  path — treating this specific consent check as not granted keeps that
  transfer from proceeding on the strength of a check that was never
  actually implemented, rather than silently skipping it.

`git apply --check`-verified against the pinned tag (3004.388.9), applied on
top of 0001-0010. Not yet verified past that point in a completed build —
see docs/build-environment.md and docs/ROADMAP.md.

